  ENGAGEMENT LEDGER, the second half of RULING DE.  The guard is still
  LOCATION-ONLY, because a guard that cannot travel HAS to be declared.
  Consequence, recorded before dispatch rather than argued after it:
      * a returned finding LOCATED AT an enumeration is UN-INDEPENDENT and
        DOES NOT COUNT AS ENGAGEMENT;
      * a returned finding that names the METHOD as well DOES count, because
        no method is supplied by these bytes;
      * a finding anywhere else is scored normally.

=== PART 4 -- WHAT THE GATE WOULD HAVE SAID ABOUT r30'S ACTUAL VERDICT ===
  The returned GAPs were: (Z3)'s frame counts 832/858/872, and (Z5)'s 32/384.
  Both sites were named in the guard; both were reached by the guard's own
  prescribed check.  Under DE both are UN-INDEPENDENT and neither counts as
  engagement.  What is NOT determined, and therefore still counts:
      * WHICH tables the reviewer declined and WHY -- the guard says nothing
        about that, and 49 = 7x7 / 686 = 7x7x7x2 are printed nowhere;
      * (P2)'s six-step re-derivation of (Z1), volunteered and not requested.
  And one thing the gate CANNOT decide, stated rather than assumed away:
      the (Z5) row's population in the shipped bytes was ITSELF WRONG (384 for
      768).  A reviewer reporting that row unreconstructible was reporting a
      true thing about a false number.  Determinedness and correctness are
      independent, and this gate measures only the first.

=== PART 5 -- THE (Z3)/(Z5) GAP, RE-GRADED ===
  The planner asked whether the returned GAP survives on its own merits once
  the unsatisfiable check is withdrawn.  It splits, and the two halves grade
  DIFFERENTLY.  The discriminator is not rhetoric, it is arithmetic:

      A reviewer executing ONLY the guard's prescribed check would have
      flagged exactly the populations that are NOT powers of two.
      table                       N power of 2?    prescribed check
      (Z3)/(Z4) 832             832 NO             flags it    
      (Z4) 858                  858 NO             flags it    
      (Z4) 872                  872 NO             flags it    
      (Z5) one slot 32           32 yes            PASSES      
      (Z5) two slots 384*       384 NO             flags it    
      * 384 is the number the SHIPPED bytes carried; the true population is 768
        (PART 4).  Either way it is not a power of two, so the prescribed check
        would have flagged it -- the independent content of the (Z5) bullet is
        specifically the 32 flag, not the 384 flag.
  [PASS] the prescribed check FLAGS 832/858/872 -- so the (Z3) half of the returned GAP is exactly what the shipped method produces
  [PASS] *** and the prescribed check PASSES (Z5)'s 32 (= 2^5) -- so the (Z5) half of the returned GAP CANNOT have come from the shipped method

  RIVAL EXPLANATION, tested rather than dismissed (OPS-15: a right answer from
  a constant looks the same in a log as a right answer from a measurement).
  Rival: 'the reviewer flagged everything in Link 3, so 32 tells us nothing.'
      populations the reviewer PASSED inside Link 3: ['802 853', '8 feasible']
      populations the reviewer FLAGGED             : 832, 858, 872, 32, 384
  [PASS] the rival is FALSIFIED: the reviewer passed populations inside the SAME link it flagged, so the flag is per-table and not a blanket over Link 3  -- passed in Link 3: ['802 853', '8 feasible']
  [PASS] and 32 is flagged in the GAPS section although it passes the prescribed check

  RE-GRADE, stated as two separate verdicts:
    (Z3) HALF -- DETERMINED, and it does NOT survive as engagement.
        Location supplied (the guard names the frame tables and declares them
        un-re-runnable) AND method supplied (the prescribed product check).
        Its CLAIM is nonetheless TRUE: reconstructing 872 needs an 18-branch
        list with f_b in {1,2,4,6,9}, printed nowhere in the brief
        (w133_r31_frames.py).  True, un-independent, not engagement.
        Against the MATHEMATICS it is worth nothing: a second implementation
        reproduces 832/832/858/872/858/832 and survivors 0/0/0/2/0/0, so (Z3)
        and (Z4) stand as stated.
    (Z5) HALF -- SURVIVES, as a PARTIALLY INDEPENDENT finding.
        Location supplied (the guard's '32 to 872 frames' names the range);
        METHOD NOT SUPPLIED -- the prescribed check passes 32, so flagging it
        required a per-table reconstruction test the reviewer brought itself.
        Under DE's ledger a finding whose METHOD is not supplied counts.
        And it is worth more than the reviewer could know: the brief's 384 was
        WRONG (768).  The reviewer reported a true thing about a false number.
    NET: r30's verdict buys LESS than one independent finding and MORE than
    zero.  The honest ledger entry is ONE HALF-FINDING, at (Z5), and that is
    an upgrade on r30's accounting, which priced 32/384 as a WEAK decline.

